    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nBehind solid timber gates, Seascape offers a rare sense of privacy and exclusivity in one of South County Dublin's most desirable coastal suburbs. Built approximately sixteen years ago, this detached home combines the assurance of a modern build with the maturity and comfort that only time can bring. Its position overlooking a large green creates an immediate feeling of openness, while the views stretching across Dublin Bay towards the Poolbeg chimneys provide a daily reminder of the beauty of its setting.\n\nInside, the house is thoughtfully arranged to support both relaxed family living and easy entertaining. The ground floor features a welcoming living room and a bright kitchen/breakfast room, complemented by a guest W.C. and a practical cloak hanging area. On the first floor, three well proportioned bedrooms offer excellent flexibility, with one enjoying its own en suite shower room alongside a family bathroom. The fourth bedroom occupies the second level, creating a superb private suite with an additional en suite shower room, ideal for guests, older children, or a peaceful home office.\n\nThe exterior of the property is equally appealing. There is generous off street parking behind the timber gates, and the rear garden has been designed for low maintenance enjoyment, laid mainly in lawn with a patio area perfect for outdoor dining. Two side passages provide convenient access between the front and rear of the house. The open aspect to the front, overlooking the expansive green, offers a wonderful space for children to play and enhances the sense of space and light throughout the property.\n\nThe location is one of the home's greatest strengths. Dalkey Heritage Town is only a short stroll away, offering an exceptional selection of specialised shops, cafés, restaurants, and pubs, along with the DART station providing swift access to Dublin City Centre and destinations around the bay. Families will appreciate the choice of highly regarded primary and secondary schools in the surrounding area. For those who love the outdoors, Dalkey's coastal walks are among the finest in Ireland, with routes taking in Dalkey and Killiney Hill, Dalkey Quarry, the Vico Road, and Coliemore Harbour. The area is also well served by the Aircoach and several Dublin Bus routes, ensuring excellent connectivity.\n\n9A Mapas Road represents a rare opportunity to secure a private, modern home in a prestigious and vibrant coastal community, an address that offers not just a place to live, but a lifestyle to savour."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 1.65m x 3.15m\nwith solid wooden floor, enclosed fuse board, intercom system and recessed lighting\n\nInner Hall - 3.8m x 1.1m\nwith understairs storage cupboard and cloak hanging area\n\nCloakroom/Guest W.C. - 1.5m x 1.9m\nwith w.c., wash hand basin, heated towel rail, tiled floor and partially tiled walls\n\nLiving Room - 5.5m x 3.8m\nwith solid wooden floor, bay window, open fireplace with sandstone surround, polished granite inset and polished granite hearth, sliding double doors lead to the\n\nKitchen/Dining Room - 3.5m x 7.1m\n(overall) 3.5m x 7.1m (11'6\" x 23'4\")\n\nDining Room - 3.5m x 3.8m\nwith solid wooden floor, double doors to the rear garden\n\nKitchen - 3.5m x 3.5m\nwith a range of cupboards and units, polished granite work surfaces, sink unit, plumbed for washing machine, integrated Bosch dishwasher, Potterton gas boiler, integrated four ring Nordmende gas hob with Whirlpool extractor fan over, integrated eye level Whirlpool double electric oven, integrated Beko fridge/freezer and polished tiled floor\n\nFirst Floor - \n\n\nLanding - \nwith recessed lighting\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.25m x 5.7m\nwith fitted wardrobes and\n\nEn Suite Shower Room - 2.7m x 1.45m\nwith step in double tray shower with monsoon head over, wash hand basin, w.c., tiled floor, partially tiled walls, heated towel rail and recessed lighting\n\nBedroom 2 - 2.7m x 3.9m\nwith fitted wardrobes\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.75m x 3.1m\n\n\nBathroom - 2.6m x 2m\nwith bath with shower over, w.c., wash hand basin with cupboards under, heated towel rail and tiled floor\n\nSecond Floor - \n\n\nBedroom 4 - 4.85m x 4.5m\nwith a range of fitted wardrobes, eave storage, two Velux windows with fabulous views over the Dublin roof tops, Dublin Bay and Killiney Hill, two window seats with storage and\n\nEn Suite Shower Room - 1.8m x 2.5m\nwith step in shower with monsoon head over, w.c., wash hand basin, tiled floor, heated towel rail, partially tiled walls and recessed lighting\n\nStorage Cupboard/Plantroom - 1.2m x 3m\nvery good storage cupboard with access to eave storage\n\n"
      },
